r the Cloverfield  paradox is real and they are in an  alternate dimension with their situation  now understood the Cloverfield  scientists begin working on a solution  to return to their own dimension the key  to their plan is an algorithm developed  by engineer Tam but repairing the  station proves to be extremely dangerous  both Tam and Mundi are killed in the  process of mending the Cloverfield and  Commander Kiel sacrifices himself to  eject part of the station so the rest of  it will hold together in the film's most  emotional plotline Hamilton discovers  that her children are still alive in  this version of Earth she decides to  stay in the alternate universe to keep  her children safe despite the fact that  there's another version of herself  already living there suddenly Jenson  violently turns on the crew she knocks  out Hamilton fatally shoots the station  dr. monk and wounds the German engineer  Schmidt after Hamilton wakes up Jenson  explains that she can't allow the  station to leave because she needs the  Shepherd to save her version of the  world the two began a fight to the death  that ultimately ends when Jenson is  sucked out of a broken window into space  Hamilton then decides that she must  return home to her own dimension because  the children from this earth are not  replacements for her own with Jensen  dead Hamilton makes a video message for  her alternate self she warns her about  the accident that killed her own  children and sends detailed plans for  how to rebuild the successful version of  the Sheppard which will save her world  Hamilton and a wounded Schmidt returned  the Cloverfield station to their  original dimension and reactivate the  Shepherd beam as they reestablished  communication with earth they announced  that the accelerator is finally working  properly and they head home in a capsule  craft while all this has been happening  Hamilton's husband Michael has been  dealing with some serious problems on  earth when the Sheppard